    <modified>2026-10-30T13:06:41Z</modified>
	<content type="text/html" mode="escaped">Author: &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.smspower.org:443/forums/profile.php?mode=viewprofile&amp;u=27589&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;old_pirate&lt;/a&gt;&lt;br /&gt;
	Posted: Fri Oct 30, 2026 1:06 pm (GMT 0)&lt;br /&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;span class="postbody"&gt;
	&lt;blockquote&gt;  &lt;div class=&quot;attribution&quot;&gt;sverx wrote    &lt;script type=&quot;text/javascript&quot; src=&quot;./templates/select_expand_bbcodes.js&quot;&gt;&lt;/script&gt;    &lt;script type=&quot;text/javascript&quot;&gt;    &lt;!--        var id = 'SXBB' + (1000 + Math.floor(Math.random() * 5000));        SXBB[id] = new _SXBB(id);        SXBB[id].T['select'] = 'Select';        SXBB[id].T['expand'] = '[+]';        SXBB[id].T['contract'] = '[-]';        SXBB[id].writeCmd();    //--&gt;    &lt;/script&gt;  &lt;/div&gt;  &lt;div class=&quot;body&quot;&gt;    &lt;script type=&quot;text/javascript&quot;&gt;      &lt;!--        SXBB[id].writeDiv();      //--&gt;    &lt;/script&gt;@old_pirate: can you provide more details about the porting process (and was it AI-assisted or not) ?    &lt;script type=&quot;text/javascript&quot;&gt;      &lt;!--        document.write('&lt;/div&gt;');      //--&gt;    &lt;/script&gt;  &lt;/div&gt;&lt;/blockquote&gt;
&lt;br /&gt;
While I relied solely on my own intuition when creating &lt;a href=&quot;https://old-pirate.itch.io/battle-city-sms&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; class=&quot;postlink&quot;&gt;Battle City&lt;/a&gt;, this time I made use of the game's decompilation for the NES. I also utilized AI, which guided me on how to implement a light gun for the SMS. Furthermore, the AI ​​handled the sound effects—a task I personally dislike the most when it comes to video game development.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br /&gt;
	</content>
